%S A399715 1,1,2,1,3,2,1,4,2,3,1,5,3,2,4,1,6,3,5,2,4,1,7,4,2,6,3,5,1,8,4,6,2,7,
%T A399715 3,5,1,9,5,3,7,2,8,4,6,1,10,5,8,3,7,2,9,4,6,1,11,6,3,9,5,8,2,10,4,7,1,
%U A399715 12,6,9,3,11,5,8,2,10,4,7
%N A399715 T(n,k) is the k-th term obtained by greedily selecting the smallest number in {1..n} whose sorted distances to previously selected terms are lexicographically maximal, triangle read by rows.
%C A399715 The "urinal sequence" arises in the etiquette of choosing from rows of devices such as urinals and treadmills (see Reddit link).
%H A399715 Bence Hervay, <a href="/A399715/b399715.txt">Rows n=1..100 of triangle, flattened</a>
%H A399715 Reddit, <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/funny/comments/8e4rdb/proper_urinal_etiquette_assuming_the_door_is_on/">Proper urinal etiquette</a>
%e A399715 Triangle begins:
%e A399715   n\k 1  2  3  4  5  6  ...
%e A399715   1   1;
%e A399715   2   1, 2;
%e A399715   3   1, 3, 2;
%e A399715   4   1, 4, 2, 3;
%e A399715   5   1, 5, 3, 2, 4;
%e A399715   6   1, 6, 3, 5, 2, 4;
%e A399715   ...
%e A399715 Row 5, T(5, 1..5), has the following interpretation:
%e A399715 - 1st person chooses 1, as all positions tie, so the smallest is preferred;
%e A399715 - 2nd person chooses 5, furthest from the 1st person;
%e A399715 - 3rd person chooses 3, the middle one (largest minimum distance from the other two);
%e A399715 - 4th person chooses 2, same sorted distances as 4, but smaller is preferred;
%e A399715 - 5th person chooses 4, the only remaining position.
%t A399715 T[n_,k_]:=Last@Nest[Function[a,a~Append~Last@SortBy[Range@n~Complement~a,{Sort@Abs[#-a],-#}&]],{},k]
%o A399715 (Python)
%o A399715 def build_row(n):
%o A399715     row = []
%o A399715     while len(row) < n:
%o A399715         best = max(
%o A399715             set(range(1, n + 1)) - set(row),
%o A399715             key=lambda x: (sorted(abs(x - y) for y in row), -x)
%o A399715         )
%o A399715         row.append(best)
%o A399715     return row
%o A399715 print([Tnk for n in range(1, 101) for Tnk in build_row(n)])
%K A399715 nonn,tabl,new
%O A399715 1,3
